# Playwright screenshot baselines are BINARY. `binary` expands to
# -diff -merge -text, so git never tries a textual (or eol-mangled) diff of a
# ~45KB PNG: `git diff` reports "Binary files differ" and the rendered PNG diff
# in the PR's Files tab stays THE review artifact for a visual change - which
# is the whole point of committing these files. Without this a stray
# `core.autocrlf` / `.gitattributes` normalization could also corrupt them.
/test/e2e/*.spec.ts-snapshots/*.png binary
